<div id="2026-09-02-hdry-stl-mislink-fix" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-02 — HDRY: four L1 corners pointed at L2 STLs + STL volume parser was 3.3x high</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Fixed four <code>printing_3d_models</code> rows that were linked to the WRONG STL, and fixed a Perl <code>unpack()</code> bug that made every computed STL volume ~3.3x too large.<br>
Mis-linked rows (L1 named, L2 geometry): model 32 FL01&rarr;FL02.stl, 22 BL01&rarr;BL02.stl, 26 BR01&rarr;BR02.stl, 20 BBR01&rarr;BBR02.stl. The correct L1 files existed on disk under wrong names: <b>FL03.stl IS FL01</b>, BL03 IS BL01, BR03 IS BR01, BBR03 IS BBR01.<br>
Volumes/weights backfilled for 19 rows that had none (including the 4 repaired ones).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> BambuStudio 3MFs ship <b>UNNAMED</b> objects (verified 39/30/20/33 objects, zero name attributes across the four plates). The importer had no object&rarr;part mapping, guessed names from plate heuristics producing only <code>02</code>/<code>03</code> numbering, then silently fell back to a near-name match. Inventory items and BOM lines were still created for all four L1 corners, so rows existed with correct names but wrong files — every "download FL01" actually served FL02 geometry. That is why downloads asked to <em>replace</em>.<br>
Separately, <code>unpack('f&lt;3 f&lt;3 f&lt;3 f&lt;3')</code> does NOT group as intended in Perl; it silently mis-parses. It reported 446.73 cm&sup3; for a part whose true volume is 137.20 cm&sup3;, inflating every filament estimate derived from <code>parse_stl</code>. Fixed to <code>unpack('f&lt;12', ...)</code>; now matches Python ground truth 20/20 on both bbox and volume.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>How proven.</strong> L1 corners are 150 mm tall, L2 215 mm (rule holds 20/20). Ambiguous files resolved by mirror-geometry + Z-scale chamfer matching against known-good L2 corners: 1.67x&ndash;2.82x separation, clean 4-of-4 bijection. <b>FR01 (model 36) was already correct</b> — the one L1 corner that imported properly.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> New <code>lib/Comserv/Util/PartGeometry.pm</code> (validator: refuses any link whose geometry contradicts the part name; 24/24 on the test suite). New <code>script/hdry_repair_part_links.pl</code> (validated, idempotent, dry-run default). Fixed <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Printing3d.pm</code> <code>parse_stl</code> (the unpack bug). Audit + reusable detectors in <code>hdry_work/STL_EXTRACTION_AUDIT.md</code>, <code>hdry_work/stl_audit.py</code>, <code>hdry_work/crosscheck.py</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Known remaining gaps (not fixed).</strong> Model 31 FLS02 has no path (<code>FLS02_.stl</code> exists on disk, trailing underscore); model 46 SRL01b has no file at all; models 38/40 point at door variants; BBL01 has duplicate rows (ids 17, 18) with different volumes; extraction shortfall vs source objects (Module_1 39&rarr;36, Extras 33&rarr;21).</p>
</div>
